id: pm-web-fy9a
title: Expand pm-web coverage gate to every executable source file and all four 100% metrics
description: "The current release:check passed 408 real-Postgres and other tests, but coverage-gate reported only 32 source files with several measured branch/function percentages below 100. This does not meet the requested all-source 100/100/100/100 quality gate. The existing pm-web-9ulj issue specifically owns route-layer real-Postgres integration; this item owns gate scope and all four metrics across every executable source file."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T12:36:48.604Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-29T12:36:48.604Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "Measure and require 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines for every executable source file; retain real integration and route tests; fail when a file is omitted or coverage data is missing; avoid artificial tests or coverage exclusions."
reporter: codex
severity: medium
environment: "pm-web PR #163 release:check 2026-09-29; coverage-gate 32 reported source files"
repro_steps: npm run coverage; inspect the per-file coverage table and scripts/coverage-gate.ts source inclusion and thresholds.
expected_result: "All executable TypeScript source files are included and statements, branches, functions, and lines each measure 100% through real behavior tests."
actual_result: Current gate says thresholds met for 32 source files while several per-file metrics are below 100 and executable source outside that declared set is unmeasured.
